From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add a PCIe suspend OPP

Give pcie0 a suspend-only OPP so pcie-qcom keeps a nonzero DDR/LLCC
sleep-set contract once the CPU subsystem collapses in s2idle. Without
it pcie-qcom votes 0/0 on the PCIe memory path during suspend. When no
other subsystem holds a DDR vote (for example the ADSP with no audio
stream open), the device does not resume from the collapse and resets
instead of waking.

Same memory floor as the SM8550 companion: 1000 kBps peak, of the same
order as the vendor kernel's 800 kBps PCIe suspend vote.

The cpu-pcie path votes 0. Its 1 kBps kept the config NoC (CN0) in the
RPMh sleep set for the whole sleep, and the link is down in suspend so
nothing reaches the PCIe registers. CN0 is a keepalive BCM, so the
active and wake sets still get a floor vote before resume touches them.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -5620,6 +5620,17 @@
 					opp-peak-kBps = <1969000 1>;
 				};
 
+				/*
+				 * Suspend-only: the synthetic opp-hz and missing opp-level
+				 * keep link-speed matching from selecting it. Only the
+				 * memory path keeps a sleep vote; cpu-pcie drops to 0.
+				 */
+				opp-suspend-1 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1>;
+					required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <1000 0>;
+					opp-suspend;
+				};
 			};
 
 			pcieport0: pcie@0 {
